<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Calvert, 1st Baron Baltimore</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1580–1632</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Calvert, 1st Baron Baltimore, was an English politician who served as Secretary of State to James I before resigning in 1625 on his conversion to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a>. He founded the Colony of Avalon at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferryland">Ferryland</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/newfoundland">Newfoundland</a> in 1621 but found its climate too harsh. He then sought a charter for a colony further south, which was granted to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cecil-calvert">Cecil Calvert</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a> shortly after his death in 1632.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-calvert-1st-baron-baltimore.jpg" alt="George Calvert, 1st Baron Baltimore" width="320" height="507" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Daniël Mijtens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Baron_George_Calvert_by_Daniel_Mytens_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
